WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.967
(happy music plays)

00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:05.693
(whooshing)

00:00:05.693 --> 00:00:07.488
- I'm Dr. John Sessa, I'm
the executive director

00:00:07.488 --> 00:00:09.442
of the Vanderpump Dog Foundation.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:12.274
And we are here at our brand new shelter

00:00:12.274 --> 00:00:13.662
in West Hollywood.

00:00:13.662 --> 00:00:15.911
Really the whole idea of this shelter

00:00:15.911 --> 00:00:18.854
is to re image the shelter
and re image a shelter dog.

00:00:18.854 --> 00:00:20.634
So we bring in dogs from kill shelters

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.496
that don't necessarily look their best.

00:00:22.496 --> 00:00:24.174
They were neglected, they have a lot

00:00:24.174 --> 00:00:26.286
of rehabilitation and PTSD issues.

00:00:26.286 --> 00:00:27.916
Immediately when the dogs come in,

00:00:27.916 --> 00:00:30.687
after they're quarantined and
we do our health assessment,

00:00:30.687 --> 00:00:32.325
we get them Vanderpuffed.

00:00:32.325 --> 00:00:35.264
And so that allows them
to have a new image

00:00:35.264 --> 00:00:37.441
and we've noticed that
it really does improve

00:00:37.441 --> 00:00:39.064
the way that they walk around.

00:00:39.064 --> 00:00:40.300
They feel a lot better.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.133
So now we're gonna get two

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.706
of our newest rescues Vanderpuffed.

00:00:42.706 --> 00:00:43.809
So let's go meet 'em.

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:45.954
- My name is Hannah, I'm
the adoption coordinator

00:00:45.954 --> 00:00:49.363
here at Vanderpump Dogs,
and this is Buster.

00:00:49.363 --> 00:00:51.665
Buster was from a high kill shelter.

00:00:51.665 --> 00:00:54.624
On his card it said that
he was an owner surrender,

00:00:54.624 --> 00:00:56.828
that means that his owner
didn't want him anymore

00:00:56.828 --> 00:00:58.659
or couldn't take care of him anymore.

00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:02.548
If he was not rescued, he
probably would've been euthanized.

00:01:02.548 --> 00:01:04.450
He's pretty dirty but we're gonna take him

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.370
and get him all cleaned up
and ready to be adopted.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:10.855
- This is someone very
special. This is Dewey.

00:01:10.855 --> 00:01:13.049
One of our rescuers who
goes to the shelters for us

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:16.326
actually saw Dewey get
thrown from a vehicle.

00:01:16.326 --> 00:01:19.948
Dewey was obviously in a
very neglected situation

00:01:19.948 --> 00:01:24.240
so his coat is matted,
he has fleas and ticks,

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.515
he's very dirty, and
he's gonna get a makeover

00:01:27.515 --> 00:01:29.729
and surly he's nervous now,

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:31.982
but he's gonna get used to his new home

00:01:31.982 --> 00:01:34.638
and eventually get a permanent home.

00:01:34.638 --> 00:01:36.251
So let's go get them Vanderpuffed.

00:01:36.251 --> 00:01:38.415
- So typically when we get these guys in,

00:01:38.415 --> 00:01:40.799
we do a full assessment on their coats,

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:44.161
and their ears, and their teeth

00:01:44.161 --> 00:01:49.078
and just to see what the
condition of the dog is in.

00:01:49.078 --> 00:01:52.216
We give 'em a bath, and clipping,

00:01:52.216 --> 00:01:54.472
and conditioner, and a blow dry,

00:01:54.472 --> 00:01:56.759
and they look as good as new.

00:01:56.759 --> 00:01:57.907
Right buddy?

00:01:57.907 --> 00:02:00.907
(happy music plays)

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:26.034
(whooshing)

00:02:38.462 --> 00:02:40.795
(whooshing)

00:02:57.165 --> 00:02:59.279
- So now that we've put
on the finishing touch,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.347
we're gonna go and make sure

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:01.831
that these guys are spayed and neutered

00:03:01.831 --> 00:03:03.849
so that they're ready to
go to their forever home.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:05.336
- Thanks for hangin'
out with us today guys.

00:03:05.336 --> 00:03:08.419
(happy music plays).

00:03:11.426 --> 00:03:12.259
Bye.

00:03:22.225 --> 00:03:26.392
(whooshing)
(creaking)

